{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01UDkvQAzqh8ccgjKjGevDF7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Anchor is a single-user productivity + R&D control system for J.C. Liechty, living entirely in `C:\\dev\\Anchor`. Grounded from the project docs:\n\n- **It's a personal task/project manager backed by plain markdown.** Markdown files are the source of truth (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, `domains/*.md`, `CANCELLED.md`, `SAVED_FOR_LATER.md`) â€” no database. Tasks move through a lifecycle (active â†’ done â†’ cancelled â†’ saved-for-later â†’ restored) with optional notes.\n\n- **It ships as a persistent local web app.** `anchor_gui.py` is a stdlib-only Python HTTP server that renders the full dashboard on every request and writes directly to the markdown files. It runs continuously as the NSSM Windows service `anchor` on `http://localhost:8777`. A CLI engine (`anchor.py`) mirrors the same logic and also generates a static `dashboard.html`.\n\n- **It has grown a multi-generation \"R&D control surface\" for trio-driven development** (the researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman skill trio). v2 added a session model, cached/validated summaries, a Grass Catchers idea lane, deliverable pinning, and an interactive terminal. v3 \"Mission Control\" added real ConPTY terminals, per-session git-worktree isolation, a stacking window manager, stage handoffs, runnable deliverable previews, and Ghost World Labs branding. v4 \"Project Cockpit\" (built + merged to master 2026-06-13) reworks each project window into a calm single-screen cockpit: lane tiles with status lights, inline expanding summary+terminal panels, a claudeâ†”gemini engine toggle, per-lane doc roles, cost/tokens/time rollups, grassâ†’lane promotion, and type-aware deliverable launch.\n\n- **Its North Star (locked) is the cockpit feel:** each lane (Research Â· Planning Â· Build) shows its most-recent session as a tile with one honest status light (green=working Â· amber=needs-you Â· red=crashed Â· grey=idle/done); clicking expands an inline panel â€” never a new page â€” stacking a summary above a real resizable terminal, and opening a session feels exactly like a normal Claude Code / Gemini session (skill auto-loads once, greets once, no repeating-prompt loop).\n\n- **It's strictly stdlib-only with one declared exception.** The whole product uses Python stdlib except the terminal subsystem's optional `pywinpty` (lazy `import winpty`, in `pty_manager.py` only, a `pip install .[terminal]` extra that degrades gracefully if absent). `distro.py`'s import scan enforces this.\n\n- **It self-tests daily.** `anchor_healthcheck.py` runs at 5:00 AM via Task Scheduler, parsing every markdown file, booting a throwaway server, exercising every endpoint, walking a synthetic task through all states, and walking the fully-stubbed v2/v3/v4 R&D surfaces (never live `claude`, never touching the live `:8777` service or real data); it writes a report and flags failures with a red dashboard banner."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4412,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":45306,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ad11a883-277e-4836-a5c1-66a9d3c8ace4","uuid":"78fc37f9-63df-40ed-a86c-a97bcb3fcde7","request_id":"req_011Cc1fAyGz2q5FKiRPNkHGa"}
