ession as a tile with one honest status light (green=working Â· amber=needs-you Â· red=crashed Â· grey=idle/done); clicking expands an inline panel â€” never a new page â€” stacking a summary above a real resizable terminal, and opening a session feels exactly like a normal Claude Code / Gemini session (skill auto-loads once, greets once, no repeating-prompt loop).\n\n- **It's strictly stdlib-only with one declared exception.** The whole product uses Python stdlib except the terminal subsystem's optional `pywinpty` (lazy `import winpty`, in `pty_manager.py` only, a `pip install .[terminal]` extra that degrades gracefully if absent). `distro.py`'s import scan enforces this.\n\n- **It self-tests daily.** `anchor_healthcheck.py` runs at 5:00 AM via Task Scheduler, parsing every markdown file, booting a throwaway server, exercising every endpoint, walking a synthetic task through all states, and walking the fully-stubbed v2/v3/v4 R&D surfaces (never live `claude`, never touching the live `:8777` service or real data); it writes a report and flags failures with a red dashboard banner.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"ad11a883-277e-4836-a5c1-66a9d3c8ace4","total_cost_usd":0.074502,"usage":{"input_tokens":4412,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":45306,"output_tokens":1139,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4412,"output_tokens":1139,"cache_read_input_tokens":45306,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":1234,"outputTokens":16,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.001314,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-8[1m]